{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>It shall be holy to you.</b> Its produce is subject to the law of sacred food. One might think it could go out to profane use — Scripture says <b>תהיה</b> — it must remain in its sacred state (Sifra; Sukkah 40a)." "<b>From the field you shall eat.</b> By means of the field you eat from the house — for if the food in the field is used up, you must clear out [what is] in the house. Just as is stated regarding the seventh year, so is stated regarding the Jubilee (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:14.677107171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}